# The gallery: what the engine can do, side by side on one board, behind the
# main menu. Seven worlds in rock frames, every one a pack of its own, all
# compiled together as one rule set (every name is global, so none collide):
#
#   x 1..192,    y 1..214     a farm: hens, foxes, bees and flowers by a river, lakes and ponds
#                             (the built-in kinds; the terrain drawn from smooth noise)
#   x 194..321,  y 1..64      two Gosper guns firing past each other into eaters, pulsars, galaxies
#                             and a pentadecathlon (packs/life)
#   x 323..382,  y 1..64      a cyclic automaton of 16 colours: spirals (packs/cyclic)
#   x 194..321,  y 66..129    rule 90 from one cell, the Sierpinski triangle, redrawn as its
#                             springs pick again (packs/elementary)
#   x 323..382,  y 66..129    Langton's ant and an LLRR ant (packs/turmite)
#   x 194..321,  y 131..214   a grove of L-system trees that wither and grow again (packs/lsystem)
#   x 323..382,  y 131..214   the 5-state busy beaver drawn as its history, starting over at
#                             its panel's edge (packs/turing)
#
# Two columns right of the farm, split at x = 322: the left one 128 cells
# wide, the right one 60.
#
#   make run ARGS="play saves/gallery --scenario scenarios/gallery.scenario"
#
# The boards that start full are shares in a region (`start K N / D in ...`);
# the gun and the pen are drawn. The `run` and `expect` lines at the end check
# that the worlds run side by side as each does alone.
rules ../rules ../packs/life ../packs/turing ../packs/elementary ../packs/cyclic ../packs/turmite ../packs/lsystem
seed 1
outside rock
